title: 'statement gossip: route v2 DHT propagation through the per-peer outbox'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, statements the orchestrator targets at a peer
    now go through the same per-peer outbox as v1 propagation: one chunk in flight per peer,
    the shared in-flight byte budget, a bounded queue and a retry after a failed store fetch.
    The outbox serves a peer the statements its affinity filter matches and those it is a DHT
    routing target for, the same set the initial sync replays. A queued statement that left
    the store or expired before its chunk went out, or was still queued when the peer
    disconnected, is counted in `undelivered_statements` under `missing_from_store` or
    `disconnected`.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
